To use this project, install MATLAB with the Statistics and Machine Learning Toolbox (R2016b or newer), then put the script, train.csv and test.csv together in one folder. Open MATLAB, set that folder as the current folder, and open the script. Click Run, or type the script name in the Command Window. The script loads both files, builds the weather summary and building history features, trains the gradient boosting model, and predicts energy use for every building in the test file. When it finishes, it saves a file called test_predictions.csv in the same folder, with one row per building showing its id and predicted site EUI. Training can take a few minutes because the dataset has about 75,000 rows. If MATLAB can’t find the data, check that the file names match exactly and that your current folder is the one containing them.
